Name: fuchsia.hardware.ethernet (banjo)
License: BSD-style (see file copyright headers)
Upstream: https://fuchsia.googlesource.com/fuchsia
Upstream path: sdk/banjo/fuchsia.hardware.ethernet
Revision: 0f3c21bc
Fetched via: gitiles +archive
  https://fuchsia.googlesource.com/fuchsia/+archive/0f3c21bc/sdk/banjo/fuchsia.hardware.ethernet.tar.gz

Vendored-at-baseline. ethernet.fidl is verbatim from upstream @ 0f3c21bc. BUILD.bazel is
authored for Cerise (a direct clone of the sibling fuchsia.hardware.pciroot BUILD.bazel,
names retargeted); the upstream BUILD.gn is kept alongside for reference and is NOT used.

This is the legacy DFv1 EthernetImpl/EthernetIfc banjo protocol. The only consumer in this
tree is the realtek-8111 driver
(src/upstream/fuchsia/src/connectivity/ethernet/drivers/realtek-8111). The FIDL depends
only on zx (the vdso), so the generated C++ banjo bindings
(fuchsia.hardware.ethernet_banjo_cpp) build with the existing Cerise banjo toolchain.
